---The scheduling configuration for a queue. Defines the strategy used to assign workers to jobs.
---@class aws.deadline.SchedulingConfiguration
---@field priorityFifo? aws.deadline.PriorityFifoSchedulingConfiguration Workers are assigned to the highest-priority job first. When multiple jobs share the same priority, the job submitted earliest receives workers first. This is the default scheduling configuration for new queues.
---@field priorityBalanced? aws.deadline.PriorityBalancedSchedulingConfiguration Workers are distributed evenly across all jobs at the highest priority level. When workers cannot be evenly divided, the extra workers are assigned to the jobs submitted earliest. If a job has fewer remaining tasks than its share of workers, the surplus workers are redistributed to other jobs at the same priority level.
---@field weightedBalanced? aws.deadline.WeightedBalancedSchedulingConfiguration Workers are assigned to jobs based on a weighted formula that considers job priority, error count, submission time, and the number of tasks currently rendering. Each factor has a configurable weight that determines its influence on scheduling decisions.

---The weight applied to the number of errors on a job in the weighted balanced scheduling formula.
---@alias aws.deadline.SchedulingErrorWeight number

---Defines the override behavior for jobs at the maximum priority (100) in weighted balanced scheduling.
---@class aws.deadline.SchedulingMaxPriorityOverride
---@field alwaysScheduleFirst? aws.deadline.SchedulingMaxPriorityOverrideAlwaysScheduleFirst Jobs at the maximum priority (100) are always scheduled before other jobs, regardless of the weighted scheduling formula. If multiple jobs have priority 100, ties are broken using the standard weighted formula.

---Specifies that jobs at the maximum priority (100) are always scheduled first.
---@class aws.deadline.SchedulingMaxPriorityOverrideAlwaysScheduleFirst

---Defines the override behavior for jobs at the minimum priority (0) in weighted balanced scheduling.
---@class aws.deadline.SchedulingMinPriorityOverride
---@field alwaysScheduleLast? aws.deadline.SchedulingMinPriorityOverrideAlwaysScheduleLast Jobs at the minimum priority (0) are always scheduled after all other jobs, regardless of the weighted scheduling formula. If multiple jobs have priority 0, ties are broken using the standard weighted formula.

---Specifies that jobs at the minimum priority (0) are always scheduled last.
---@class aws.deadline.SchedulingMinPriorityOverrideAlwaysScheduleLast

---The weight applied to job priority in the weighted balanced scheduling formula.
---@alias aws.deadline.SchedulingPriorityWeight number

---The rendering task buffer used in balanced scheduling.
---@alias aws.deadline.SchedulingRenderingTaskBuffer number

---The weight applied to the number of rendering tasks in the weighted balanced scheduling formula.
---@alias aws.deadline.SchedulingRenderingTaskWeight number

---The weight applied to job submission time in the weighted balanced scheduling formula.
